--   ```
--
--   **Context.** KIL4: the offset table generator with run-time stage data
--
--   KIL2's `genP Q ac` has one stage per field of the prefix `A` of the target, every number (`Q`,
--   the radix `a`, the control `c`, the suffix volume `M`) a literal.  The uniform generator `genPU n`
--   reads the stages from four stage stacks (`34 … 37`: `a`, `c`, `M`, `a·M`, the last stage on top) and
--   `-Q` from the parameter stack `23`; its code depends only on the number `n` of stages.
--
--   * `gStageT`, `rsim_gStage`: the stage as a template; the literal stage simulates it.
--   * `stagesU_sp`, `genPU_sp`: the generator pushes `tbl Q ac` on stack `14`, pops the stage stacks.
--   * `tbl_zeros`, `tbl_app_congr`: the table only depends on the controls; runs of control-`0`
--     fields collapse to one field of their volume (the "collapsed" stage lists of the uniform
--     shifts have at most `2m + 3` stages whatever the shape).
